# Docker build context is the repo root (see infra/web.Dockerfile). Without this
# file, `COPY . .` drags the local, multi-gigabyte `.next/` build cache into the
# image. `next build` then emits a fresh webpack runtime whose chunk map does not
# match the stale chunk files left behind, so dynamic imports (e.g. cesium) fail
# at runtime with ChunkLoadError and the globe never mounts. Keep build inputs to
# source only; deps are reinstalled (`npm ci`) and `.next` is produced clean.

# Build outputs / caches (the cause of the chunk-mismatch bug)
**/.next/
**/.turbo/
**/dist/
**/out/

# Dependencies (reinstalled in-image via npm ci)
**/node_modules/

# Python virtualenvs + caches (engine venv is large; web build never needs them)
**/.venv/
**/__pycache__/
**/*.pyc
**/.pytest_cache/
**/.ruff_cache/
**/.mypy_cache/

# VCS + local tooling artifacts
.git/
.gstack/
graphify-out/
**/*.log
